{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FRXHe5GjC85gbPUCmDeKex","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Wii Fit 2007 game features Body Test Wii Fit Age Balance Board character Fit Piggy Bank yoga strength aerobics balance games\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Wii Fit\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wii_Fit\"},{\"title\":\"cavac.at\",\"url\":\"https://cavac.at/cavacopedia/Wii%20Fit\"},{\"title\":\"nintendoworldreport.com\",\"url\":\"https://nintendoworldreport.com/preview/13858\"},{\"title\":\"Prerelease:Wii Fit\",\"url\":\"https://new.tcrf.net/Prerelease:Wii_Fit\"},{\"title\":\"Wii Fit\",\"url\":\"https://www.wikipedia.com/wiki/Wii_Fit\"},{\"title\":\"Wii Fit\",\"url\":\"https://gamicus.fandom.com/wiki/Wii_Fit\"},{\"title\":\"Wii Fit\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Wii_Fit\"},{\"title\":\"Wii Fit\",\"url\":\"https://ultimatepopculture.fandom.com/wiki/Wii_Fit\"},{\"title\":\"Wii Fit (Nintendo Wii, 2007-2008) - ohne Brett - Spiel, Hülle, Booklet dabei-\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebay.de/itm/312856787143\"},{\"title\":\"e3 2007 wii balance board\",\"url\":\"https://www.nintendolife.com/news/2007/07/e3_2007_wii_balance_board\"},{\"title\":\"e3 2007 wii fitness\",\"url\":\"https://www.nintendolife.com/news/2007/07/e3_2007_wii_fitness\"},{\"title\":\"wii fit\",\"url\":\"https://www.timeextension.com/games/wii/wii_fit\"},{\"title\":\"Wii Fit\",\"url\":\"https://wii.fandom.com/wiki/Wii_Fit?oldid=4080\"},{\"title\":\"Archives by Day\",\"url\":\"https://worthplaying.com/article/2007/7/16/previews/43513/\"},{\"title\":\"Title Wii Fit\",\"url\":\"https://awards.cesa.or.jp/2009/en/prize/year/14.html\"},{\"title\":\"Wii Fit\",\"url\":\"https://bafybeiemxf5abjwjbikoz4mc3a3dla6ual3jsgpdr4cjr3oz3evfyavhwq.ipfs.4everland.io/wiki/Wii_Fit.html\"},{\"title\":\"Wii Fit\",\"url\":\"https://ipfs.ssi.eecc.de/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Wii_Fit\"}]\n\nWii Fit was a 2007 exergaming game from Nintendo, released in Japan on December 1, 2007, and it is built around the Wii Balance Board. The search results support most of your feature list, though not the Fit Piggy Bank.\n\n- **Activities:** The game's mini-games span yoga, strength training, aerobics, and balance. One source says it offers over 40 activities, and another lists the yoga poses Deep Breathing, Half-Moon, and Warrior. It features a variety of yoga, strength training, aerobics, and balance mini-games for use with the Wii Balance Board peripheral.\n- **Body Test:** This measures body mass index and balance. Each Body Test determines and updates the player's \"Wii Fit Age\", which loosely suggests the player's physical strength in relation to their true age. One source adds that the board also checks the player's center of balance and posture.\n- **Balance Board:** The board measures weight and center of balance, and it's the only required peripheral. Wii Fit requires the use of the Wii Balance Board, a unique platform peripheral that the player stands upon during play.\n- **Scoring:** When the activity ends, the player is scored based on how well the player kept their balance during the session. Points are deducted if the player's body haphazardly swayed or shook at any point.\n- **Profiles:** One source says the game allows up to eight different profiles to be registered.\n- **Fit Piggy Bank:** None of the results mention this feature, so I couldn't confirm it.\n\nA follow-up, Wii Fit Plus, came out in October 2009 with about twenty new games and activities.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19933fd7-aa65-437e-a4da-e4509b9efb8a","uuid":"b3696eb5-6213-481a-b716-204ef5cf6b8d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:57:21.229Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Wii Fit 2007 game features Body Test Wii Fit Age Balance Board character Fit Piggy Bank yoga strength aerobics balance games","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013WN2BzqSALFszvi1AA9Htx","content":[{"title":"Wii Fit","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wii_Fit"},{"title":"cavac.at","url":"https://cavac.at/cavacopedia/Wii%20Fit"},{"title":"nintendoworldreport.com","url":"https://nintendoworldreport.com/preview/13858"},{"title":"Prerelease:Wii Fit","url":"https://new.tcrf.net/Prerelease:Wii_Fit"},{"title":"Wii Fit","url":"https://www.wikipedia.com/wiki/Wii_Fit"},{"title":"Wii Fit","url":"https://gamicus.fandom.com/wiki/Wii_Fit"},{"title":"Wii Fit","url":"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Wii_Fit"},{"title":"Wii Fit","url":"https://ultimatepopculture.fandom.com/wiki/Wii_Fit"},{"title":"Wii Fit (Nintendo Wii, 2007-2008) - ohne Brett - Spiel, Hülle, Booklet dabei-","url":"https://www.ebay.de/itm/312856787143"},{"title":"e3 2007 wii balance board","url":"https://www.nintendolife.com/news/2007/07/e3_2007_wii_balance_board"},{"title":"e3 2007 wii fitness","url":"https://www.nintendolife.com/news/2007/07/e3_2007_wii_fitness"},{"title":"wii fit","url":"https://www.timeextension.com/games/wii/wii_fit"},{"title":"Wii Fit","url":"https://wii.fandom.com/wiki/Wii_Fit?oldid=4080"},{"title":"Archives by Day","url":"https://worthplaying.com/article/2007/7/16/previews/43513/"},{"title":"Title Wii Fit","url":"https://awards.cesa.or.jp/2009/en/prize/year/14.html"},{"title":"Wii Fit","url":"https://bafybeiemxf5abjwjbikoz4mc3a3dla6ual3jsgpdr4cjr3oz3evfyavhwq.ipfs.4everland.io/wiki/Wii_Fit.html"},{"title":"Wii Fit","url":"https://ipfs.ssi.eecc.de/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Wii_Fit"}]},"Wii Fit was a 2007 exergaming game from Nintendo, released in Japan on December 1, 2007, and it is built around the Wii Balance Board. The search results support most of your feature list, though not the Fit Piggy Bank.\n\n- **Activities:** The game's mini-games span yoga, strength training, aerobics, and balance. One source says it offers over 40 activities, and another lists the yoga poses Deep Breathing, Half-Moon, and Warrior. It features a variety of yoga, strength training, aerobics, and balance mini-games for use with the Wii Balance Board peripheral.\n- **Body Test:** This measures body mass index and balance. Each Body Test determines and updates the player's \"Wii Fit Age\", which loosely suggests the player's physical strength in relation to their true age. One source adds that the board also checks the player's center of balance and posture.\n- **Balance Board:** The board measures weight and center of balance, and it's the only required peripheral. Wii Fit requires the use of the Wii Balance Board, a unique platform peripheral that the player stands upon during play.\n- **Scoring:** When the activity ends, the player is scored based on how well the player kept their balance during the session. Points are deducted if the player's body haphazardly swayed or shook at any point.\n- **Profiles:** One source says the game allows up to eight different profiles to be registered.\n- **Fit Piggy Bank:** None of the results mention this feature, so I couldn't confirm it.\n\nA follow-up, Wii Fit Plus, came out in October 2009 with about twenty new games and activities."],"durationSeconds":5.466919642999768,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FRXHe5GjC85gbPUCmDeKex","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
