{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDLcbL5qL25hb9eVqvh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011dmZQWgJxrL1p2Zo1G2UGC","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211856__x2e2035/work/PLAN.md","offset":1,"limit":240},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1652,"cache_read_input_tokens":577281,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1652},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19933fd7-aa65-437e-a4da-e4509b9efb8a","uuid":"b6a35f81-8660-4d88-9b81-18316c9b2ede","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:16:40.680Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDLcHThUSXdg4Zftnce","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011dmZQWgJxrL1p2Zo1G2UGC":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211856__x2e2035/work/PLAN.md","offset":1,"limit":240}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011dmZQWgJxrL1p2Zo1G2UGC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Game plan: a balance-and-wellness comedy inspired by Wii Fit\n2\t\n3\tYou will build this game from this plan alone. The director is not available for questions.\n4\t\n5\t## 0. How to read this plan\n6\t\n7\t- **Your brief** means the brief in your own working folder. It wins on the title method, file and folder names, dates, the deliverables and the feedback questions. This plan names none of them.\n8\t- **Paths** are relative to the dev folder your brief tells you to create. Clone the engine to `engine/` inside it.\n9\t- **Numbers** are starting values. Tune them with the dev sliders and the bot. The structure is decided; change it only if it fails in play.\n10\t- **Gaps:** if something is not covered, decide, write one line in `notes/decisions.md`, and carry on.\n11\t- **Verified** means it was run on this computer on 2026-11-04, against engine commit `49ef2ba` and AI Hub client 1.4.0. Section 15 lists those results.\n12\t- **Title:** pick it first, the way your brief says. Keep it in one constant. This plan calls it \"the game\". The resort's name, Tippy Cay, belongs to the world and does not depend on the title.\n13\t- **Reading cost:** you do not need to read the engine's source to start. Read `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` whole (about 3k tokens) and `engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/starter.rs`, then use this plan. Search `engine/docs/REFERENCE.md` and `engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` when you need a tool or a prop field.\n14\t\n15\t## 1. The game in one page\n16\t\n17\tYou have won a five-day stay at Tippy Cay, a small wellness resort staffed entirely by talking gym equipment. You do not remember entering. Each morning a relentlessly pleasant wobble cushion tests your balance and gives you a Balance Age. Each day you walk the island, try short stillness, strength, cardio and balance events, and bank minutes in a giant clam. Checkout requires a Balance Age of 40 or better. Day 5 ends in the Big Stand, a finale whose last test is to do nothing at all for thirty seconds while the game tries to make you press something.\n18\t\n19\t- **Genre:** sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame (daily ritual, unlocks, wardrobe). Catalogue genre: Sports.\n20\t- **Perspective:** third person throughout, with a camera chosen per activity: 3/4 follow on the island, a mirror-style front view for exercises on the spot, chase for the jog and the paddle, high 3/4 for the table, side view for the dives.\n21\t- **Length:** a first run takes 25 to 40 minutes. It shows every feature. Free play follows.\n22\t\n23\t| What makes Wii Fit distinctive | How this game turns it into play |\n24\t|---|---|\n25\t| A balance board: your centre of pressure is the only verb, and tiny movements matter | The Balance Core (section 4): one analog dot driven by lean. Every event is played through it |\n26\t| The body test and the verdict of a fitness age | The Morning Wobble Check and Balance Age. Never weight, BMI or body shape |\n27\t| Equipment that talks: cheerful, polite, quietly rude | Pip, a talking wobble cushion, plus a whole staff of talking gear |\n28\t| A calm, uncanny instructor | Posey, a faceless wooden artist's mannequin |\n29\t| Four disciplines: yoga, strength, aerobics, balance games | Four pavilions, each with its own coach and events |\n30\t| The daily ritual: calendar stamps, banked minutes that unlock more | Calendar stamps and the Minute Clam |\n31\t| Noticing how long you stayed away | Real-date absence comments from Pip |\n32\t| A family sharing one board and comparing progress | Hot-seat Medley, Yesterday You ghosts, AI Hub sessions |\n33\t| Clean, quiet, pastel, unintentionally funny | High-key pastel look, gentle lounge music, short deadpan text |\n34\t\n35\t**Pillars.** Check every decision against these.\n36\t1. **Small movements, big consequences.** Mastery means doing less. The best moments are held breaths.\n37\t2. **Deadpan encouragement.** Everything you do is commented on, kindly, and slightly too honestly.\n38\t3. **A daily ritual.** Check in, get a number, do your exercises, get a stamp.\n39\t4. **Calm surface, silly underneath.** The screen stays serene while a seagull stands on your head.\n40\t\n41\t**Originality rules.** This is an original game in the same genre, not a recreation.\n42\t- Inside the game, use no Nintendo names (Wii, Mii, Balance Board and so on). The only exceptions are the Source line on the About screen and whatever your title's riff requires.\n43\t- No white rectangular board with dot eyes. No pale human trainer in a tank top and ponytail. No Mii-style avatars or face editors. No island or plaza from the source series.\n44\t- No source music, jingles, menu layouts or screen compositions. Do not quote or paraphrase its lines. Write your own.\n45\t- Events have their own names and twists, as specified below.\n46\t- Respect bodies: no weight, BMI, body-shape jokes or diet talk anywhere. Pip judges your wobble, your habits and your absences.\n47\t\n48\t## 2. Structure of play\n49\t\n50\t**Boot:** title screen over a slow island sweep. Menu: New Stay or Continue, Play Together, Settings, About. After 10 seconds with no input on the title or any pre-game menu, attract mode starts (section 12).\n51\t\n52\t**New Stay:** choose one of 4 guest slots, pick a name from a list of about 40 funny preset names (no on-screen keyboard), pick a look (6 skin tones, 8 outfits). Then a short intro with Pip at reception, skippable.\n53\t\n54\t**A day:**\n55\t1. Wake on the cabana deck. Pip greets you, with an absence comment if real days have passed.\n56\t2. Morning Wobble Check (about 70 seconds), Balance Age reveal, Pip's comment.\n57\t3. Free time on the island: walk, talk to guests, find lost flip-flops, step on an event mat. The Schedule (Triangle or Tab) lists everything and fast-travels.\n58\t4. When the day's minute goal is met, Pip says so. Sleep at your cabana (or choose End Day in the Schedule). A big stamp lands on the Calendar. Next day.\n59\t\n60\t| Day | Opens | Minute goal | Story beat |\n61\t|---|---|---|---|\n62\t| 1 | Stillness Studio: Breath Bloom, Pose Parade | 3 | Arrival. The checkout rule. \"Nobody has asked to leave yet\" |\n63\t| 2 | Iron Gazebo: Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff | 5 | Big Kettle. Wardrobe opens |\n64\t| 3 | Boardwalk: Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap | 7 | Yesterday You appears as a ghost. \"I am not comparing you\" |\n65\t| 4 | Lagoon: Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup | 9 | Guests start whispering about the Big Stand |\n66\t| 5 | The Big Stand, after the morning check | none | Finale, ending, free play |\n67\t\n68\t**Minutes:** the first clear of an event each day banks 1 + stars (0 to 3 stars, so 1 to 4 minutes); repeats bank 1. Resort minutes are openly not real minutes (\"Our minutes are longer. It is a wellness thing\").\n69\t\n70\t**Endings:** Balance Age 40 or better: you may check out, by rowboat (`LIB/core/rowboat`). Otherwise: the Extended Stay ending, gentle and funny. Both roll credits, then unlock Free Play: every event open, personal bests, star goals, and a calendar that keeps stamping real days.\n71\t\n72\t**Bot rule:** `Game::bot` must be able to play this entire flow, menus included, from New Stay to the credits. That is your scripted playthrough and the base of attract mode.\n73\t\n74\t## 3. Controls\n75\t\n76\tThe left stick is both walking and leaning. Prompts always show the glyph for the input used last.\n77\t\n78\t| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n79\t|---|---|---|---|\n80\t| Walk on the island, lean in events | Left stick | W A S D (arrows also walk) | Island: click a place or thing to walk there. Events: cursor offset from screen centre is the lean |\n81\t| Fine lean | Stick itself | Hold Shift (half key rate) | Small cursor moves |\n82\t| Jog on the island | Hold R2 | Hold Shift | |\n83\t| Action: talk, begin, inhale, squat, bounce | Cross | Space | Left button |\n84\t| Left step / right step | L1 or L2 / R1 or R2 | Q or Left / E or Right | Left button / right button |\n85\t| Brace (hold both) | L2+R2 or L1+R1 | Q+E | Both buttons |\n86\t| Wave at someone | Square | F | |\n87\t| Schedule | Triangle | Tab | |\n88\t| Island camera | Right stick | | Right-drag, wheel zooms |\n89\t| Pause | Options | Esc | |\n90\t| Menus | D-pad or left stick, Cross confirms, Circle backs, L1/R1 change tabs | Arrows or W A S D, Enter or Space, Esc backs, Q/E change tabs | Hover moves focus, click activates, right-click backs |\n91\t\n92\tXbox glyphs (Settings option) swap A B X Y, LB RB LT RT, Menu. Ignore Options while Create is held: that pair belongs to the AI Hub. Disable the engine's own keys (F1 to F10, digits, H, Backspace rewind, right-drag tilt) outside dev mode. Keep F11 for fullscreen.\n93\t\n94\t## 4. The Balance Core\n95\t\n96\tOne struct, `BalanceCore`, used by every event. Its state is `cob` (the dot, unit disc, x right, y up on screen) and `vel`.\n97\t\n98\t```\n99\ttarget = shaped lean input\n100\tacc    = (target - cob) * stiffness - vel * damping + wobble + gust + nudge\n101\tvel   += acc * dt\n102\tcob   += vel * dt\n103\ttip    = |cob| > 1 for tip_time seconds\n104\t```\n105\t\n106\tStart with `stiffness 18`, `damping 7`, `tip_time 0.35`. `wobble` is two sines (1.3 Hz and 2.9 Hz, phases from `sim.state.rng`) plus a small random impulse every 1 to 2 seconds, base amplitude `0.10`, scaled per event and by fatigue. Use sim time, never the clock.\n107\t\n108\t**Feel targets:** full stick reaches the rim in about 0.35 s. Release settles in about 0.5 s with a slight overshoot, like a body. A skilled player holds the dot within radius 0.1 under base wobble using tiny corrections.\n109\t\n110\t**Input shaping** (in `pav_app`, passed as `InputFrame.lean`, screen space):\n111\t- **Stick:** deadzone 0.12, response curve `x^1.5` so small motions are fine.\n112\t- **Keyboard:** keys move the target at 1.6 units/s and it returns at 1.2 units/s when released. Tapping gives small nudges, so keys feel native, not bang-bang.\n113\t- **Mouse:** cursor offset from the screen centre divided by 0.38 of the window height, clamped to the disc. No pointer lock. The device moved last wins.\n114\t\n115\t**Body:** the figure tilts with the dot (`cob * 14` degrees about the feet, engine change in section 14). Beyond |cob| 0.75 an upper-body arm-flail clip fades in. A tip plays a stumble and, over water, a splash. Tips never end the game; they cost time or score.\n116\t\n117\t**HUD, the Puck:** a large circular gauge drawn in egui: a pale disc, a green target ring, a coral dot, and stars at the edge when streaking. It must read from 10 feet. It looks good at 340 px diameter at 1080p (verified). Put it top centre or bottom centre, whichever does not cover the figure in that event.\n118\t\n119\t## 5. Events\n120\t\n121\t**Common frame:** event card (name, one-sentence goal, glyph prompts, one coach line), 3-2-1, play, result (score 0 to 1000, stars at 400, 650 and 850, a deadpan Title, minutes banked, personal best, difference from Yesterday You; Retry or Back).\n122\t\n123\t**Every event has:** a section of tunable numbers in `rules.toml`, a bot that earns at least 2 stars, an idle-input outcome below 1 star, a ghost lane, and an attract segment. Scenes `fit/event/<name>` start an event directly, for tools and tests.\n124\t\n125\t### Stillness Studio (Posey). Set: `studio`, a round white deck on a calm dawn lagoon. Camera: mirror view (yaw 0, tilt 12, distance 8.5, fov 36; the figure faces +Z, toward the camera, and stick right is screen right).\n126\t\n127\t**Breath Bloom** (45 s). Hold Action to inhale, release to exhale, following a guide ring: 4 s in, 4 s out, 5 cycles, the last one longer. `lungs` rises while held and falls when not. Keep the dot inside a centre ring of radius 0.35. Tick score: `0.7 * (1 - clamp(|lungs - guide| / 0.35)) + 0.3 * inRing`. Each good cycle opens a lotus on the water with a rising pentatonic chime; a perfect run blooms the whole pond. Scrub the clip `FIT/Breath` by `lungs`. No fail state. Bot: holds while the guide rises.\n128\t\n129\t**Pose Parade** (3 poses, 20 s each). Six hand-keyed poses with deadpan names: the Patient Heron, the Apologetic Lunge, the Tired Lighthouse, the Folded Deck Chair, the Reluctant Bridge, Seated Disappointment. Day 1 uses the first three. Posey holds the pose beside you. A target ring (radius 0.30 shrinking to 0.18) drifts on a slow Lissajous path (amplitude 0.35, 0.12 Hz). Inside the ring a streak multiplier climbs x1 to x4, one step per 2 s; leaving resets it. At 12 s of pose 2 a gull lands on your head and wobble is x1.6 for 5 s (\"There is a bird on you. Accept the bird\"). A tip breaks the pose for 1.5 s. Score: time in ring weighted by multiplier. Bot: PD toward the ring centre.\n130\t\n131\t### Iron Gazebo (Big Kettle). Set: `gazebo`, a white iron gazebo at golden hour. Camera: 3/4 front.\n132\t\n133\t**Tempo Squats** (10 reps, about 50 s). Hold Action to go down (2 s to full depth), release to rise (1 s). A guide bar shows the tempo; a low bell marks the bottom. Keep the dot in a band |x| < 0.25; wobble grows 8% per rep. Rep score: `0.7 * timing + 0.3 * band`. Scrub `FIT/Squat` by depth. Gag: rep 10 is followed by \"Ten. Also eleven.\" Bot: follows the guide.\n134\t\n135\t**Plank Standoff** (up to 60 s). Hold Brace and keep the dot in a ring shrinking from 0.40 to 0.20. Releasing, or leaving the ring for more than 1 s, collapses you in a comic flop. Fatigue ramps wobble; at 30 s add tremble; at 45 s Kettle laughs at his own joke and the nudge shakes the screen. Score: seconds survived / 60. Stars at 25, 40 and 55 s. Kettle, who has no arms, plank-talks you through it. Base the pose on one frame of `MESH2MOTION/Pushup`. Bot: survives at least 45 s.\n136\t\n137\t### Boardwalk (Bounce). Set: `boardwalk`, a beach boardwalk at bright midday.\n138\t\n139\t**Step Party** (64 s, 96 BPM, song 4). A rhythm game: notes in two lanes fall to two footprints, left, right or both, on an aerobic step box. Perfect within 55 ms, Good within 120 ms. About 100 notes, data in `charts.toml`, starting with quarter notes and building to eighths and doubles. Bounce bounces on the beat and guests clap on downbeats. Timing uses the audio clock (section 10). Camera: mirror view, slightly high. Bot: presses exactly on each note.\n140\t\n141\t**Floatie Spin** (50 s). Circle the lean (stick, mouse, or rolling W-D-S-A) to spin inflatable rings around your hips. Spin speed is the smoothed angular velocity of the lean while |lean| > 0.4; the sweet band is 6 to 9 rad/s, and a `spin_band_scale` rule widens it for keyboard. \"Switch!\" flips the required direction every 15 s. Guests toss new rings from left or right: press that side's step within 0.25 s of arrival to catch it. Out of band, rings sink; on the floor they are lost. Maximum 7 rings. Score: rings times time in band. Rings are no-physics entities positioned in code. Bot: 7.5 rad/s circle, presses on arrivals.\n142\t\n143\t**Morning Lap** (about 90 s, one lap of the hub island). Alternate left and right steps to set your pace (1.6 to 2.4 steps/s is the zone). Too fast raises a stitch meter that makes you stumble; too slow and Bounce, the pacer rolling ahead, gets away. The path steers you; lean moves you up to 1.2 m sideways to dodge crabs, sunbathers and towels and to grab ribbons. Flip-flops can be found here too. Score: time in zone, plus ribbons, minus bumps. Camera: chase with per-tick yaw. Use `MESH2MOTION/Jog` scaled to speed. Bot: 2 steps/s, steers to ribbons.\n144\t\n145\t### Lagoon (Commodore Gull). Sets: `tide`, `channel`, `pier`, `tower`.\n146\t\n147\t**Tide Table** (3 boards, 60 s total). You stand on a floating square raft and your lean tilts it. Roll hermit crabs in shells into tide pools. Board 1: 3 shells. Board 2: 5 shells and a moving pool. Board 3: 7 shells, bumpers and a rising tide. Fast shells skip over pools. Write the shell physics as simple 2D code (`a = tilt * g - friction * v`, wall bounce 0.5), not rapier: it is more tunable and bot-friendly. Score: shells potted plus time left. Camera: high 3/4 (tilt 62). Bot: PD steering of the nearest shell toward the nearest pool.\n148\t\n149\t**Paddle Slalom** (about 45 s). Stand on a paddleboard on a long channel and pass buoy gates. Lean x steers. Lean forward speeds up and risks tipping, lean back brakes. Gusts, shown as ripple streaks, push the dot. A tip is a big splash and a 2 s remount. A missed gate adds 2 s. `score = clamp((1.6 * par - t) / (0.8 * par)) * 1000`. Standing on water uses the trick in section 15; a silent `Wake` event every few ticks draws the wake. Camera: chase (tilt 22, distance 10). Bot: steers to gate centres at forward lean 0.5.\n150\t\n151\t**Tray Trek** (about 50 s). Walk a long pier at a fixed pace, carrying a tray with a stack of 5 smoothies. Waves, plank gaps and swooping gulls jolt the tray. Your dot tilts it. Glasses slide with tilt and plop into the sea past the edge. Score: 200 per glass delivered, plus a no-spill bonus. Marjorie receives what is left and comments. Use `STYLE100/Balance_Walk` plus an upper-body `FIT/CarryTray` clip. Bot: counters the jolts it knows are coming.\n152\t\n153\t**Cannonball Cup** (3 dives, about 40 s). The board bounces with a 1.2 s period. Press Action at the bottom of 3 bounces to build power, the 4th press leaps. In the air, hold Action to tuck and lean to rotate. Enter tucked and high for the biggest splash. Three gull judges hold up cards: \"6.5\", \"7\", \"See me\". \"We are not here for form. We are here for splash.\" Score: height x tuck x timing. Camera: side view (yaw 90, tilt 6, distance 14). The splash must be huge: a new `BigSplash` event scales the water dents and particles. This is the attract mode's hero shot. Bot: presses on bottoms, tucks at the apex.\n154\t\n155\t### The Big Stand (finale, about 2.5 minutes). Set: `bay`, a tiny post in the bay at sunset, with the whole cast watching from rafts.\n156\t\n157\tFive phases, reusing event code with new numbers:\n158\t1. Breathing, 4 cycles.\n159\t2. A pose under rising gusts, 20 s.\n160\t3. Step Party for 16 bars with a marching band of guests, wobble on.\n161\t4. Brace while waves crash, 20 s.\n162\t5. **The Long Stillness:** 30 s of nothing. Music fades to silence, the HUD vanishes except the Puck. At 15 s a fake prompt offers \"Press Cross to skip\". Pressing anything forfeits the Inner Peace bonus. Then Pip, quietly: \"...Oh. You're still here. Good.\"\n163\t\n164\tA tip drops you in the sea to a groan from the crowd and puts you back; it costs score and cannot end the run. Final Balance Age = morning age minus `final_score / 100` (up to 10).\n165\t\n166\t### Morning Wobble Check. Set: `studio`. About 70 s, four micro-tests, Pip presiding.\n167\t\n168\t| Test | What you do | Metric (0 to 1) |\n169\t|---|---|---|\n170\t| Stand Still (\"This is the whole test\") | Hold the dot centred for 8 s; one small nudge at 5 s | Mean distance from centre |\n171\t| Lean Targets | A left/right bar: reach \"70% left\", then two more targets, within 6%, hold 1.5 s; 5 s limit each | Time taken |\n172\t| Eyes Closed | 6 s. The screen dims to almost black, the Puck vanishes. A tone's pitch tells your offset, and rumble if the pad has it | Mean distance |\n173\t| Step Test | 8 alternating steps to a 100 BPM metronome | Timing |\n174\t\n175\t```\n176\tskill = 0.30*still + 0.25*targets + 0.25*blind + 0.20*steps\n177\tage   = 24 + 56 * (1 - skill)^1.1 - 2*days_completed - min(total_stars/3, 8)\n178\t```\n179\tClamp to 18..99, round. The big number rolls like a slot machine. Pip's comment is chosen by the change since yesterday and by the worst metric. A sparkline of 5 big dots shows the week. Your figure's posture improves as the age falls (a small constant forward slump through the tilt field, shrinking each day): visible progress, no numbers needed.\n180\t\n181\t## 6. Meta systems\n182\t\n183\t- **Minute Clam:** a giant clam at reception that gulps banked minutes with a gibberish burp. Totals unlock wardrobe items.\n184\t- **Calendar:** five big days, a stamp per completed day, then real days in free play. No tables.\n185\t- **Titles:** after each event Pip awards a deadpan title by score: Human Soup, Acceptable Human, Certified Lean-To, Wobble Enthusiast, Seasoned Tilter, Stillness Intern, Professional Standing Person, Alarmingly Balanced. At least 30, in `script.toml`.\n186\t- **Wardrobe:** reuse the engine's `GearLook`, which needs no new drawing (verified): `helm = cap` (sun cap), `helm = hood` (towel turban), `crown`, `halo`; `gloves` (sweatbands), `belt`, `pauldrons` (reads as arm floaties, funny). Plus shirt, pants and shoe colours. Skip `cape`: it draws long sticks.\n187\t- **Lost flip-flops:** 5 hidden on the island, for Two-Towel Tom. Reward: Golden Flip-Flops (gold shoes) and a line. This is the exploration layer.\n188\t- **Yesterday You:** your best run of each event is recorded and replayed as a tinted figure in a neighbouring lane, from Day 3.\n189\t- **Absence comments:** the page passes today's date to the game at boot, and the save stores the last day played. \"You were away for 2 days. I did not count them. There were 2.\" Passing the date in as data keeps the rule that the sim never reads the clock.\n190\t- **Saves:** versioned JSON in `localStorage`: guest slots (name, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings. Save on every change of day and every result.\n191\t\n192\t## 7. World, cast and writing\n193\t\n194\t**Tippy Cay** is about 64 x 48 m: reception at the centre (Pip's desk, Calendar wall, Minute Clam), a ring path for jogging, four pavilions around it, a row of cabanas, a pier, a diving tower and a water channel in the distance. Palms, grass, sand terraces, sea on all sides, circling gulls.\n195\t\n196\t| Character | What it is | Voice and manner |\n197\t|---|---|---|\n198\t| **Pip** | Sky-blue round wobble cushion, two dot eyes (`blob` plan, scale 0.7, squash 2.0, plus a small valve) | Front desk and scorekeeper. Relentlessly pleasant. Keeps records of everything. Never technically insults you. Squeaky rubber voice |\n199\t| **Posey** | Faceless wooden artist's mannequin (biped with eyes the colour of its skin; verified look in section 8) | Stillness. Serene, short, oddly poetic. Soft wood-block voice. It has no eyes and never blinks; \"This has not been discussed\" |\n200\t| **Big Kettle** | Cast-iron kettlebell (dark `blob` plus a torus handle part; add a `Handle` attach kind) | Strength. Booming, gentle, deeply supportive. No arms or legs, cannot do any exercise |\n201\t| **Bounce** | Huge pink exercise ball that never stops hopping (`blob`, scale 1.2, `hop`) | Cardio. Breathless bursts, no full stops |\n202\t| **Commodore Gull** | Small gull in a captain's cap: three no-physics entities, wings rotated in code | Lagoon. Dry, officious, steals snacks |\n203\t| **Marjorie** | Guest in robe and towel turban (`helm = hood`, white) | On Day 5 for eleven years. Knows everything |\n204\t| **Two-Towel Tom** | Guest with two towels | Lost his flip-flops. Asks you to find them |\n205\t| **The Twins** | Two identical guests | Do everything in unison, finish each other's words |\n206\t\n207\t**Writing style.** Short polite sentences. Upbeat. Then one line too honest. Fitness facts of doubtful use. Numbers quoted precisely, for no reason. At most 2 lines on screen at 10 feet. Every coach has at least 25 lines, Pip at least 80, guests about 8 each, per day where it matters. Keep all text in `script.toml`.\n208\t\n209\tTone anchors, all original. Use these and write more like them:\n210\t- Pip: \"Welcome! You have won a complimentary stay. You did not enter. Nobody enters.\"\n211\t- Pip: \"Please stand on me. Gently. I remember everything.\"\n212\t- Pip: \"Your Balance Age today is 61. That is a number. Numbers cannot hurt you. This one is trying.\"\n213\t- Pip: \"You leaned left 64% of the time. Is everything all right on the right?\"\n214\t- Pip: \"That was your best attempt so far. I am as surprised as you are.\"\n215\t- Pip: \"You wobbled 41 times. I stopped counting at 40, out of respect.\"\n216\t- Pip: \"Did you know? Standing still burns calories. Not many. Did you know that, though?\"\n217\t- Pip, on a long pause: \"You have been paused for 4 minutes. Pausing is not an exercise. I checked.\"\n218\t- Posey: \"Breathe in the sea. Not literally.\"\n219\t- Posey: \"Be the heron. The heron does not check the score.\"\n220\t- Big Kettle: \"Lift with your legs. I cannot. I have none. Lift for both of us.\"\n221\t- Bounce: \"Keep going keep going keep- is that your heartbeat? Mine is just air!\"\n222\t- Commodore Gull: \"That was a dive. I am legally required to say so.\"\n223\t- Marjorie: \"Day five? Oh, I'm on day five as well. Eleven years now.\"\n224\t\n225\tDialogue types out with voice blips. Action completes the line, then advances. Keep a Text Speed setting.\n226\t\n227\t## 8. Art direction\n228\t\n229\t**Base:** the engine's native look: cel-shaded rounded primitives, soft sun shadows, thin ink outlines on characters. Its big-headed toy figures already suit the tone. Take the look high-key and pastel.\n230\t\n231\t**Palette:** sky `#d6eef6`, sea `#8fdde0`, deck `#fbfaf6`, sand `#f6e7c8`, grass `#bfe6b0`, ink `#263e54`, teal accent `#46bec8`, mint `#78dcaa`, coral `#ff786e`, sun yellow `#ffd166`.\n232\t\n233\t**Base `[view]` for every set.** This exact recipe was verified to give a clean horizon. Vary sky, sun and warmth per set (dawn in the Studio, golden hour at the Gazebo, sunset in the Bay).\n234\t\n235\t```toml\n236\t[view]\n237\tsky = \"#d6eef6\"\n238\texposure = 1.0\n239\tsaturation = 0.95\n240\tbloom = 0.15"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19933fd7-aa65-437e-a4da-e4509b9efb8a","uuid":"7fda0ca9-8e21-4b03-9394-c020350ffc00","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:16:40.686Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211856__x2e2035/work/PLAN.md","content":"# Game plan: a balance-and-wellness comedy inspired by Wii Fit\n\nYou will build this game from this plan alone. The director is not available for questions.\n\n## 0. How to read this plan\n\n- **Your brief** means the brief in your own working folder. It wins on the title method, file and folder names, dates, the deliverables and the feedback questions. This plan names none of them.\n- **Paths** are relative to the dev folder your brief tells you to create. Clone the engine to `engine/` inside it.\n- **Numbers** are starting values. Tune them with the dev sliders and the bot. The structure is decided; change it only if it fails in play.\n- **Gaps:** if something is not covered, decide, write one line in `notes/decisions.md`, and carry on.\n- **Verified** means it was run on this computer on 2026-11-04, against engine commit `49ef2ba` and AI Hub client 1.4.0. Section 15 lists those results.\n- **Title:** pick it first, the way your brief says. Keep it in one constant. This plan calls it \"the game\". The resort's name, Tippy Cay, belongs to the world and does not depend on the title.\n- **Reading cost:** you do not need to read the engine's source to start. Read `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` whole (about 3k tokens) and `engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/starter.rs`, then use this plan. Search `engine/docs/REFERENCE.md` and `engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` when you need a tool or a prop field.\n\n## 1. The game in one page\n\nYou have won a five-day stay at Tippy Cay, a small wellness resort staffed entirely by talking gym equipment. You do not remember entering. Each morning a relentlessly pleasant wobble cushion tests your balance and gives you a Balance Age. Each day you walk the island, try short stillness, strength, cardio and balance events, and bank minutes in a giant clam. Checkout requires a Balance Age of 40 or better. Day 5 ends in the Big Stand, a finale whose last test is to do nothing at all for thirty seconds while the game tries to make you press something.\n\n- **Genre:** sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame (daily ritual, unlocks, wardrobe). Catalogue genre: Sports.\n- **Perspective:** third person throughout, with a camera chosen per activity: 3/4 follow on the island, a mirror-style front view for exercises on the spot, chase for the jog and the paddle, high 3/4 for the table, side view for the dives.\n- **Length:** a first run takes 25 to 40 minutes. It shows every feature. Free play follows.\n\n| What makes Wii Fit distinctive | How this game turns it into play |\n|---|---|\n| A balance board: your centre of pressure is the only verb, and tiny movements matter | The Balance Core (section 4): one analog dot driven by lean. Every event is played through it |\n| The body test and the verdict of a fitness age | The Morning Wobble Check and Balance Age. Never weight, BMI or body shape |\n| Equipment that talks: cheerful, polite, quietly rude | Pip, a talking wobble cushion, plus a whole staff of talking gear |\n| A calm, uncanny instructor | Posey, a faceless wooden artist's mannequin |\n| Four disciplines: yoga, strength, aerobics, balance games | Four pavilions, each with its own coach and events |\n| The daily ritual: calendar stamps, banked minutes that unlock more | Calendar stamps and the Minute Clam |\n| Noticing how long you stayed away | Real-date absence comments from Pip |\n| A family sharing one board and comparing progress | Hot-seat Medley, Yesterday You ghosts, AI Hub sessions |\n| Clean, quiet, pastel, unintentionally funny | High-key pastel look, gentle lounge music, short deadpan text |\n\n**Pillars.** Check every decision against these.\n1. **Small movements, big consequences.** Mastery means doing less. The best moments are held breaths.\n2. **Deadpan encouragement.** Everything you do is commented on, kindly, and slightly too honestly.\n3. **A daily ritual.** Check in, get a number, do your exercises, get a stamp.\n4. **Calm surface, silly underneath.** The screen stays serene while a seagull stands on your head.\n\n**Originality rules.** This is an original game in the same genre, not a recreation.\n- Inside the game, use no Nintendo names (Wii, Mii, Balance Board and so on). The only exceptions are the Source line on the About screen and whatever your title's riff requires.\n- No white rectangular board with dot eyes. No pale human trainer in a tank top and ponytail. No Mii-style avatars or face editors. No island or plaza from the source series.\n- No source music, jingles, menu layouts or screen compositions. Do not quote or paraphrase its lines. Write your own.\n- Events have their own names and twists, as specified below.\n- Respect bodies: no weight, BMI, body-shape jokes or diet talk anywhere. Pip judges your wobble, your habits and your absences.\n\n## 2. Structure of play\n\n**Boot:** title screen over a slow island sweep. Menu: New Stay or Continue, Play Together, Settings, About. After 10 seconds with no input on the title or any pre-game menu, attract mode starts (section 12).\n\n**New Stay:** choose one of 4 guest slots, pick a name from a list of about 40 funny preset names (no on-screen keyboard), pick a look (6 skin tones, 8 outfits). Then a short intro with Pip at reception, skippable.\n\n**A day:**\n1. Wake on the cabana deck. Pip greets you, with an absence comment if real days have passed.\n2. Morning Wobble Check (about 70 seconds), Balance Age reveal, Pip's comment.\n3. Free time on the island: walk, talk to guests, find lost flip-flops, step on an event mat. The Schedule (Triangle or Tab) lists everything and fast-travels.\n4. When the day's minute goal is met, Pip says so. Sleep at your cabana (or choose End Day in the Schedule). A big stamp lands on the Calendar. Next day.\n\n| Day | Opens | Minute goal | Story beat |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Stillness Studio: Breath Bloom, Pose Parade | 3 | Arrival. The checkout rule. \"Nobody has asked to leave yet\" |\n| 2 | Iron Gazebo: Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff | 5 | Big Kettle. Wardrobe opens |\n| 3 | Boardwalk: Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap | 7 | Yesterday You appears as a ghost. \"I am not comparing you\" |\n| 4 | Lagoon: Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup | 9 | Guests start whispering about the Big Stand |\n| 5 | The Big Stand, after the morning check | none | Finale, ending, free play |\n\n**Minutes:** the first clear of an event each day banks 1 + stars (0 to 3 stars, so 1 to 4 minutes); repeats bank 1. Resort minutes are openly not real minutes (\"Our minutes are longer. It is a wellness thing\").\n\n**Endings:** Balance Age 40 or better: you may check out, by rowboat (`LIB/core/rowboat`). Otherwise: the Extended Stay ending, gentle and funny. Both roll credits, then unlock Free Play: every event open, personal bests, star goals, and a calendar that keeps stamping real days.\n\n**Bot rule:** `Game::bot` must be able to play this entire flow, menus included, from New Stay to the credits. That is your scripted playthrough and the base of attract mode.\n\n## 3. Controls\n\nThe left stick is both walking and leaning. Prompts always show the glyph for the input used last.\n\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Walk on the island, lean in events | Left stick | W A S D (arrows also walk) | Island: click a place or thing to walk there. Events: cursor offset from screen centre is the lean |\n| Fine lean | Stick itself | Hold Shift (half key rate) | Small cursor moves |\n| Jog on the island | Hold R2 | Hold Shift | |\n| Action: talk, begin, inhale, squat, bounce | Cross | Space | Left button |\n| Left step / right step | L1 or L2 / R1 or R2 | Q or Left / E or Right | Left button / right button |\n| Brace (hold both) | L2+R2 or L1+R1 | Q+E | Both buttons |\n| Wave at someone | Square | F | |\n| Schedule | Triangle | Tab | |\n| Island camera | Right stick | | Right-drag, wheel zooms |\n| Pause | Options | Esc | |\n| Menus | D-pad or left stick, Cross confirms, Circle backs, L1/R1 change tabs | Arrows or W A S D, Enter or Space, Esc backs, Q/E change tabs | Hover moves focus, click activates, right-click backs |\n\nXbox glyphs (Settings option) swap A B X Y, LB RB LT RT, Menu. Ignore Options while Create is held: that pair belongs to the AI Hub. Disable the engine's own keys (F1 to F10, digits, H, Backspace rewind, right-drag tilt) outside dev mode. Keep F11 for fullscreen.\n\n## 4. The Balance Core\n\nOne struct, `BalanceCore`, used by every event. Its state is `cob` (the dot, unit disc, x right, y up on screen) and `vel`.\n\n```\ntarget = shaped lean input\nacc    = (target - cob) * stiffness - vel * damping + wobble + gust + nudge\nvel   += acc * dt\ncob   += vel * dt\ntip    = |cob| > 1 for tip_time seconds\n```\n\nStart with `stiffness 18`, `damping 7`, `tip_time 0.35`. `wobble` is two sines (1.3 Hz and 2.9 Hz, phases from `sim.state.rng`) plus a small random impulse every 1 to 2 seconds, base amplitude `0.10`, scaled per event and by fatigue. Use sim time, never the clock.\n\n**Feel targets:** full stick reaches the rim in about 0.35 s. Release settles in about 0.5 s with a slight overshoot, like a body. A skilled player holds the dot within radius 0.1 under base wobble using tiny corrections.\n\n**Input shaping** (in `pav_app`, passed as `InputFrame.lean`, screen space):\n- **Stick:** deadzone 0.12, response curve `x^1.5` so small motions are fine.\n- **Keyboard:** keys move the target at 1.6 units/s and it returns at 1.2 units/s when released. Tapping gives small nudges, so keys feel native, not bang-bang.\n- **Mouse:** cursor offset from the screen centre divided by 0.38 of the window height, clamped to the disc. No pointer lock. The device moved last wins.\n\n**Body:** the figure tilts with the dot (`cob * 14` degrees about the feet, engine change in section 14). Beyond |cob| 0.75 an upper-body arm-flail clip fades in. A tip plays a stumble and, over water, a splash. Tips never end the game; they cost time or score.\n\n**HUD, the Puck:** a large circular gauge drawn in egui: a pale disc, a green target ring, a coral dot, and stars at the edge when streaking. It must read from 10 feet. It looks good at 340 px diameter at 1080p (verified). Put it top centre or bottom centre, whichever does not cover the figure in that event.\n\n## 5. Events\n\n**Common frame:** event card (name, one-sentence goal, glyph prompts, one coach line), 3-2-1, play, result (score 0 to 1000, stars at 400, 650 and 850, a deadpan Title, minutes banked, personal best, difference from Yesterday You; Retry or Back).\n\n**Every event has:** a section of tunable numbers in `rules.toml`, a bot that earns at least 2 stars, an idle-input outcome below 1 star, a ghost lane, and an attract segment. Scenes `fit/event/<name>` start an event directly, for tools and tests.\n\n### Stillness Studio (Posey). Set: `studio`, a round white deck on a calm dawn lagoon. Camera: mirror view (yaw 0, tilt 12, distance 8.5, fov 36; the figure faces +Z, toward the camera, and stick right is screen right).\n\n**Breath Bloom** (45 s). Hold Action to inhale, release to exhale, following a guide ring: 4 s in, 4 s out, 5 cycles, the last one longer. `lungs` rises while held and falls when not. Keep the dot inside a centre ring of radius 0.35. Tick score: `0.7 * (1 - clamp(|lungs - guide| / 0.35)) + 0.3 * inRing`. Each good cycle opens a lotus on the water with a rising pentatonic chime; a perfect run blooms the whole pond. Scrub the clip `FIT/Breath` by `lungs`. No fail state. Bot: holds while the guide rises.\n\n**Pose Parade** (3 poses, 20 s each). Six hand-keyed poses with deadpan names: the Patient Heron, the Apologetic Lunge, the Tired Lighthouse, the Folded Deck Chair, the Reluctant Bridge, Seated Disappointment. Day 1 uses the first three. Posey holds the pose beside you. A target ring (radius 0.30 shrinking to 0.18) drifts on a slow Lissajous path (amplitude 0.35, 0.12 Hz). Inside the ring a streak multiplier climbs x1 to x4, one step per 2 s; leaving resets it. At 12 s of pose 2 a gull lands on your head and wobble is x1.6 for 5 s (\"There is a bird on you. Accept the bird\"). A tip breaks the pose for 1.5 s. Score: time in ring weighted by multiplier. Bot: PD toward the ring centre.\n\n### Iron Gazebo (Big Kettle). Set: `gazebo`, a white iron gazebo at golden hour. Camera: 3/4 front.\n\n**Tempo Squats** (10 reps, about 50 s). Hold Action to go down (2 s to full depth), release to rise (1 s). A guide bar shows the tempo; a low bell marks the bottom. Keep the dot in a band |x| < 0.25; wobble grows 8% per rep. Rep score: `0.7 * timing + 0.3 * band`. Scrub `FIT/Squat` by depth. Gag: rep 10 is followed by \"Ten. Also eleven.\" Bot: follows the guide.\n\n**Plank Standoff** (up to 60 s). Hold Brace and keep the dot in a ring shrinking from 0.40 to 0.20. Releasing, or leaving the ring for more than 1 s, collapses you in a comic flop. Fatigue ramps wobble; at 30 s add tremble; at 45 s Kettle laughs at his own joke and the nudge shakes the screen. Score: seconds survived / 60. Stars at 25, 40 and 55 s. Kettle, who has no arms, plank-talks you through it. Base the pose on one frame of `MESH2MOTION/Pushup`. Bot: survives at least 45 s.\n\n### Boardwalk (Bounce). Set: `boardwalk`, a beach boardwalk at bright midday.\n\n**Step Party** (64 s, 96 BPM, song 4). A rhythm game: notes in two lanes fall to two footprints, left, right or both, on an aerobic step box. Perfect within 55 ms, Good within 120 ms. About 100 notes, data in `charts.toml`, starting with quarter notes and building to eighths and doubles. Bounce bounces on the beat and guests clap on downbeats. Timing uses the audio clock (section 10). Camera: mirror view, slightly high. Bot: presses exactly on each note.\n\n**Floatie Spin** (50 s). Circle the lean (stick, mouse, or rolling W-D-S-A) to spin inflatable rings around your hips. Spin speed is the smoothed angular velocity of the lean while |lean| > 0.4; the sweet band is 6 to 9 rad/s, and a `spin_band_scale` rule widens it for keyboard. \"Switch!\" flips the required direction every 15 s. Guests toss new rings from left or right: press that side's step within 0.25 s of arrival to catch it. Out of band, rings sink; on the floor they are lost. Maximum 7 rings. Score: rings times time in band. Rings are no-physics entities positioned in code. Bot: 7.5 rad/s circle, presses on arrivals.\n\n**Morning Lap** (about 90 s, one lap of the hub island). Alternate left and right steps to set your pace (1.6 to 2.4 steps/s is the zone). Too fast raises a stitch meter that makes you stumble; too slow and Bounce, the pacer rolling ahead, gets away. The path steers you; lean moves you up to 1.2 m sideways to dodge crabs, sunbathers and towels and to grab ribbons. Flip-flops can be found here too. Score: time in zone, plus ribbons, minus bumps. Camera: chase with per-tick yaw. Use `MESH2MOTION/Jog` scaled to speed. Bot: 2 steps/s, steers to ribbons.\n\n### Lagoon (Commodore Gull). Sets: `tide`, `channel`, `pier`, `tower`.\n\n**Tide Table** (3 boards, 60 s total). You stand on a floating square raft and your lean tilts it. Roll hermit crabs in shells into tide pools. Board 1: 3 shells. Board 2: 5 shells and a moving pool. Board 3: 7 shells, bumpers and a rising tide. Fast shells skip over pools. Write the shell physics as simple 2D code (`a = tilt * g - friction * v`, wall bounce 0.5), not rapier: it is more tunable and bot-friendly. Score: shells potted plus time left. Camera: high 3/4 (tilt 62). Bot: PD steering of the nearest shell toward the nearest pool.\n\n**Paddle Slalom** (about 45 s). Stand on a paddleboard on a long channel and pass buoy gates. Lean x steers. Lean forward speeds up and risks tipping, lean back brakes. Gusts, shown as ripple streaks, push the dot. A tip is a big splash and a 2 s remount. A missed gate adds 2 s. `score = clamp((1.6 * par - t) / (0.8 * par)) * 1000`. Standing on water uses the trick in section 15; a silent `Wake` event every few ticks draws the wake. Camera: chase (tilt 22, distance 10). Bot: steers to gate centres at forward lean 0.5.\n\n**Tray Trek** (about 50 s). Walk a long pier at a fixed pace, carrying a tray with a stack of 5 smoothies. Waves, plank gaps and swooping gulls jolt the tray. Your dot tilts it. Glasses slide with tilt and plop into the sea past the edge. Score: 200 per glass delivered, plus a no-spill bonus. Marjorie receives what is left and comments. Use `STYLE100/Balance_Walk` plus an upper-body `FIT/CarryTray` clip. Bot: counters the jolts it knows are coming.\n\n**Cannonball Cup** (3 dives, about 40 s). The board bounces with a 1.2 s period. Press Action at the bottom of 3 bounces to build power, the 4th press leaps. In the air, hold Action to tuck and lean to rotate. Enter tucked and high for the biggest splash. Three gull judges hold up cards: \"6.5\", \"7\", \"See me\". \"We are not here for form. We are here for splash.\" Score: height x tuck x timing. Camera: side view (yaw 90, tilt 6, distance 14). The splash must be huge: a new `BigSplash` event scales the water dents and particles. This is the attract mode's hero shot. Bot: presses on bottoms, tucks at the apex.\n\n### The Big Stand (finale, about 2.5 minutes). Set: `bay`, a tiny post in the bay at sunset, with the whole cast watching from rafts.\n\nFive phases, reusing event code with new numbers:\n1. Breathing, 4 cycles.\n2. A pose under rising gusts, 20 s.\n3. Step Party for 16 bars with a marching band of guests, wobble on.\n4. Brace while waves crash, 20 s.\n5. **The Long Stillness:** 30 s of nothing. Music fades to silence, the HUD vanishes except the Puck. At 15 s a fake prompt offers \"Press Cross to skip\". Pressing anything forfeits the Inner Peace bonus. Then Pip, quietly: \"...Oh. You're still here. Good.\"\n\nA tip drops you in the sea to a groan from the crowd and puts you back; it costs score and cannot end the run. Final Balance Age = morning age minus `final_score / 100` (up to 10).\n\n### Morning Wobble Check. Set: `studio`. About 70 s, four micro-tests, Pip presiding.\n\n| Test | What you do | Metric (0 to 1) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Stand Still (\"This is the whole test\") | Hold the dot centred for 8 s; one small nudge at 5 s | Mean distance from centre |\n| Lean Targets | A left/right bar: reach \"70% left\", then two more targets, within 6%, hold 1.5 s; 5 s limit each | Time taken |\n| Eyes Closed | 6 s. The screen dims to almost black, the Puck vanishes. A tone's pitch tells your offset, and rumble if the pad has it | Mean distance |\n| Step Test | 8 alternating steps to a 100 BPM metronome | Timing |\n\n```\nskill = 0.30*still + 0.25*targets + 0.25*blind + 0.20*steps\nage   = 24 + 56 * (1 - skill)^1.1 - 2*days_completed - min(total_stars/3, 8)\n```\nClamp to 18..99, round. The big number rolls like a slot machine. Pip's comment is chosen by the change since yesterday and by the worst metric. A sparkline of 5 big dots shows the week. Your figure's posture improves as the age falls (a small constant forward slump through the tilt field, shrinking each day): visible progress, no numbers needed.\n\n## 6. Meta systems\n\n- **Minute Clam:** a giant clam at reception that gulps banked minutes with a gibberish burp. Totals unlock wardrobe items.\n- **Calendar:** five big days, a stamp per completed day, then real days in free play. No tables.\n- **Titles:** after each event Pip awards a deadpan title by score: Human Soup, Acceptable Human, Certified Lean-To, Wobble Enthusiast, Seasoned Tilter, Stillness Intern, Professional Standing Person, Alarmingly Balanced. At least 30, in `script.toml`.\n- **Wardrobe:** reuse the engine's `GearLook`, which needs no new drawing (verified): `helm = cap` (sun cap), `helm = hood` (towel turban), `crown`, `halo`; `gloves` (sweatbands), `belt`, `pauldrons` (reads as arm floaties, funny). Plus shirt, pants and shoe colours. Skip `cape`: it draws long sticks.\n- **Lost flip-flops:** 5 hidden on the island, for Two-Towel Tom. Reward: Golden Flip-Flops (gold shoes) and a line. This is the exploration layer.\n- **Yesterday You:** your best run of each event is recorded and replayed as a tinted figure in a neighbouring lane, from Day 3.\n- **Absence comments:** the page passes today's date to the game at boot, and the save stores the last day played. \"You were away for 2 days. I did not count them. There were 2.\" Passing the date in as data keeps the rule that the sim never reads the clock.\n- **Saves:** versioned JSON in `localStorage`: guest slots (name, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings. Save on every change of day and every result.\n\n## 7. World, cast and writing\n\n**Tippy Cay** is about 64 x 48 m: reception at the centre (Pip's desk, Calendar wall, Minute Clam), a ring path for jogging, four pavilions around it, a row of cabanas, a pier, a diving tower and a water channel in the distance. Palms, grass, sand terraces, sea on all sides, circling gulls.\n\n| Character | What it is | Voice and manner |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Pip** | Sky-blue round wobble cushion, two dot eyes (`blob` plan, scale 0.7, squash 2.0, plus a small valve) | Front desk and scorekeeper. Relentlessly pleasant. Keeps records of everything. Never technically insults you. Squeaky rubber voice |\n| **Posey** | Faceless wooden artist's mannequin (biped with eyes the colour of its skin; verified look in section 8) | Stillness. Serene, short, oddly poetic. Soft wood-block voice. It has no eyes and never blinks; \"This has not been discussed\" |\n| **Big Kettle** | Cast-iron kettlebell (dark `blob` plus a torus handle part; add a `Handle` attach kind) | Strength. Booming, gentle, deeply supportive. No arms or legs, cannot do any exercise |\n| **Bounce** | Huge pink exercise ball that never stops hopping (`blob`, scale 1.2, `hop`) | Cardio. Breathless bursts, no full stops |\n| **Commodore Gull** | Small gull in a captain's cap: three no-physics entities, wings rotated in code | Lagoon. Dry, officious, steals snacks |\n| **Marjorie** | Guest in robe and towel turban (`helm = hood`, white) | On Day 5 for eleven years. Knows everything |\n| **Two-Towel Tom** | Guest with two towels | Lost his flip-flops. Asks you to find them |\n| **The Twins** | Two identical guests | Do everything in unison, finish each other's words |\n\n**Writing style.** Short polite sentences. Upbeat. Then one line too honest. Fitness facts of doubtful use. Numbers quoted precisely, for no reason. At most 2 lines on screen at 10 feet. Every coach has at least 25 lines, Pip at least 80, guests about 8 each, per day where it matters. Keep all text in `script.toml`.\n\nTone anchors, all original. Use these and write more like them:\n- Pip: \"Welcome! You have won a complimentary stay. You did not enter. Nobody enters.\"\n- Pip: \"Please stand on me. Gently. I remember everything.\"\n- Pip: \"Your Balance Age today is 61. That is a number. Numbers cannot hurt you. This one is trying.\"\n- Pip: \"You leaned left 64% of the time. Is everything all right on the right?\"\n- Pip: \"That was your best attempt so far. I am as surprised as you are.\"\n- Pip: \"You wobbled 41 times. I stopped counting at 40, out of respect.\"\n- Pip: \"Did you know? Standing still burns calories. Not many. Did you know that, though?\"\n- Pip, on a long pause: \"You have been paused for 4 minutes. Pausing is not an exercise. I checked.\"\n- Posey: \"Breathe in the sea. Not literally.\"\n- Posey: \"Be the heron. The heron does not check the score.\"\n- Big Kettle: \"Lift with your legs. I cannot. I have none. Lift for both of us.\"\n- Bounce: \"Keep going keep going keep- is that your heartbeat? Mine is just air!\"\n- Commodore Gull: \"That was a dive. I am legally required to say so.\"\n- Marjorie: \"Day five? Oh, I'm on day five as well. Eleven years now.\"\n\nDialogue types out with voice blips. Action completes the line, then advances. Keep a Text Speed setting.\n\n## 8. Art direction\n\n**Base:** the engine's native look: cel-shaded rounded primitives, soft sun shadows, thin ink outlines on characters. Its big-headed toy figures already suit the tone. Take the look high-key and pastel.\n\n**Palette:** sky `#d6eef6`, sea `#8fdde0`, deck `#fbfaf6`, sand `#f6e7c8`, grass `#bfe6b0`, ink `#263e54`, teal accent `#46bec8`, mint `#78dcaa`, coral `#ff786e`, sun yellow `#ffd166`.\n\n**Base `[view]` for every set.** This exact recipe was verified to give a clean horizon. Vary sky, sun and warmth per set (dawn in the Studio, golden hour at the Gazebo, sunset in the Bay).\n\n```toml\n[view]\nsky = \"#d6eef6\"\nexposure = 1.0\nsaturation = 0.95\nbloom = 0.15","numLines":240,"startLine":1,"totalLines":633}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011dmZQWgJxrL1p2Zo1G2UGC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
